Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:13:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(gdn): preserve selected FP32 checkpoint snapshots

Source semantics: SGe189be978c1bfb50c463e6fd080a52fd4d111922. Reuse pinned upstream track_state/track_chunk_idx buffers, forwarding them through Triton GDN and all FLA wrapper layers into the existing accumulator snapshot kernel. Ordinary h/output dtype is unchanged. Only the actual CUDA wrapper declares capability; the admission gate rejects lossy pools, ReplaySSM and unsupported GDN prefill graphs.

Validation: four CPU tests execute actual wrapper bodies with leaf doubles and verify selected-buffer identity, unchanged untracked external-backend calls and unsupported/incomplete capability refusal; AST/diff checks passed. Actual hybrid/TP checkpoint and resumed feature/logit/loss/gradient GPU comparison remains pending independent validation.
